+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes when a member may cancel a pantry order, or answers a member whose cancellation was refused. A
+member may cancel a pantry order until 2 hours before its pickup slot starts; after that the app refuses. The cutoff
+exists because members cancelled minutes before pickup, after volunteers had packed their bags: in the first weeks of
+October 2026, 25 bags of fresh food were thrown away.
+
+## The cutoff
+
+Volunteers start packing 2 hours before each pickup slot. A cancellation before then costs the pantry nothing; one
+after it leaves a packed bag of milk, bread and greens on the shelf. A banner asking members to cancel earlier had run
+since summer and did not stop it, so the app now refuses a cancellation once packing has started.
+
+`can_cancel` in `larder/cancellation.py` decides, from the start of the pickup slot and the current time:
+
+| Pickup slot starts | Cancel at | Allowed |
+| ------------------ | --------- | ------- |
+| 17:00              | 14:59     | yes     |
+| 17:00              | 15:00     | no      |
+| 17:00              | 16:50     | no      |
+
+The cutoff itself is refused: at exactly 2 hours before the slot, packing has started.
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot come after the cutoff calls the pantry, and the volunteers decide what happens to the pantry
+order.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- The refusal message must give the pantry's phone number, the condition the pantry agreed to the cutoff on, but the
+  repository holds neither the message nor the number: `can_cancel` only answers yes or no. Until the message is
+  written, a refused member is not told whom to call.
+- The cutoff is fixed at 2 hours, `CUTOFF` in `larder/cancellation.py`, and does not follow the packing shift: if
+  packing starts at another time, change `CUTOFF` with it.
